  "id": "s13-delete-cascades",
  "title": "Delete cascades (D5): the legacy delete handlers and their ON DELETE CASCADE foreign keys",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D5 (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-100..103; SQL cases 114, 145). One plan and period; two activity types; specialties E and F; groups, cohorts, subjects, templates, teachers and rooms, some of them deleted before the run.",
    "Legacy side: the generated del_<Class> handlers (a direct DELETE by id; every foreign key cascades). Drupal side: the entity deletes, which apply the same cascade (ReferenceGuard).",
    "Deletes: group G2 (the teacher assignments keep G1), cohort B3 (G1 keeps B1), activity type C2 (its group GL and template AL with its assignment), specialty F (its cohort, group, subject and template), subject X (its template and assignments), room L2 (its room assignments). The run then places A1 and A2 for G1."
  ],
